@startuml
title CPU V3 revision 0.9 hardware structure

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

package "Fitted CPU V3 system (optional around the reusable core)" {
  component "Instruction fetch queue\n4 fetched/outstanding words\nstream cursors + current metadata\n4-entry x 2-word resolved-target BTC" as FetchQueue
  component "Instruction cache\n4 KiB, 2 ways x 64 sets x 16 words\n2 parity-split true-dual-port BSRAMs\n4 x 64-bit direct refill beats" as ICache
  component "Data cache\n4 KiB, 2 ways x 64 sets x 16 words\n2 parity-split true-dual-port BSRAMs\nwrite-back + direct 64-bit line I/O" as DCache
  component "Memory arbiter\none line or word owner at a time\nforwards one burst command per line" as Arbiter
  component "Related-clock SDRAM gearbox\n4 x 64-bit at 54 MHz\n8 x 32-bit at 108 MHz" as SDRAM
  component "Devices 0..7\n16 channels each" as Devices
  component "DMA / display\noptional system masters" as Masters
}

rectangle "CpuV3Core: precise, in-order, limited two-stage frontend" as Core {
  component "Fetch / execute FSM\nExecute may accept the next queued word\nprecise single retirement" as FSM
  storage "Instruction state\nPC 16, CSEG 16, four DSEG pages x 8\nPFX12 prefix\npending comparison" as ControlState
  storage "GPR file\n16 x 16-bit\ncombinational read\nsynchronous write" as GPR
  component "Integer lane\n16-bit ALU, shifts, compare\nCLZ / popcount" as IntAlu

  package "Two-word Q16.16 FPU v2 (opcodes C/D/E)" {
    component "Two-word front-end\nretained word0 supplies parked Fa/Fb\nword1 Fd / subop / len / mode" as Fe
    storage "FPR file\n2 x 512 x 32 SDPB BSRAM (2R1W)\nF0..F63 signed Q16.16\nhidden RCP/RSQRT/SINCOS tables" as FPR
    component "Scalar / vector lane ALU\n32-bit Q16.16 wrap\nADD/SUB/MIN/MAX/ABS/NEG\nFLOOR/CEIL/ROUND/TRUNC/MOV" as LaneAlu
    component "Shared RF port and lane owner\nALU/product read cursors and lane calendar\ncommon destination context\nexclusive final write-event bus" as Ports
    storage "Next-edge commit slot\none 32-bit ALU / DOTSTORE result\naddress + valid" as Commit
    component "Shared CPU/FPU multiply pipe\nsigned 36 x 36, 2 stages, II=1\n9-bit return tag" as FpuDsp
    storage "ACC\nsigned 64-bit Q32.32\nfull-product accumulate" as Acc
    component "Special path\nblocking RCP / RSQRT / SINCOS\nshared-pipe range and interpolation\nrelative result destination" as Special
  }
}

ICache --> FetchQueue : pipelined response
FetchQueue --> ICache : sequential physical lookup
FetchQueue --> FSM : queued instruction
FSM --> FetchQueue : 32-bit {CSEG, PC}
DCache --> FSM : data response
FSM --> DCache : translated physical address\n16-bit narrow requests
FSM <--> Devices : dedicated device port
ICache --> Arbiter
DCache --> Arbiter
Masters --> Arbiter
Arbiter --> SDRAM
Masters ..> ICache : invalidate
Masters ..> DCache : invalidate

FSM <--> ControlState
FSM <--> GPR
GPR --> IntAlu
IntAlu --> GPR
GPR --> FpuDsp : unsigned integer operands\nexclusive integer issue
FpuDsp --> GPR : integer result window
FSM --> Fe : two-word pair (0xC/0xD/0xE)
Fe --> FSM : word-pair complete
Fe --> Ports : accepted descriptor
GPR <--> FSM : FLD / FST base GPR[X]
FSM <--> Ports : idle ext channel (FLD / FST beats)
Ports --> FPR : two synchronous read addresses\none broadcast write
FPR --> Ports : external read return
FPR --> LaneAlu : one lane from each read port
LaneAlu --> Commit : scalar/vector result
Commit --> Ports : original next-edge write
FPR --> FpuDsp : ordinary product operands
Ports --> FpuDsp : product issue / return tag
FpuDsp --> Ports : direct tagged MUL write
FpuDsp --> Acc
Acc --> Commit : final DOTSTORE window
Special --> Ports : LUT addresses / direct write event
FPR --> Special : packed LUT read return
Special --> FpuDsp : range / interpolation products
FpuDsp --> Special : tagged return

note right of Fe
Issue policy:
* no scoreboard, forwarding, or dependency comparison
* busy and final commit close each instruction before the next one issues
* FPU instructions are fetch barriers and never consume PFX12
* scalar ALU writes at T1; vector ALU lane k writes at T(k+2)
* vector lanes retain II=1; shared multiplication has two enabled stages
* RCP/RSQRT are blocking T0..T4; SINCOS T0..T8 dual / T0..T7 single
* abort cancels pending writes; RF reads retain read-first semantics
end note

note bottom of Core
Core target-leaf resources:
* integer/FPU multiplication shares one MULT36X36 macro
* FPR leaf claim: 2 SDPB BSRAM blocks
The system composes these claims with cache, boot, display, and board resources.
end note

@enduml
